Ultimate Marvel vs Capcom 3 NX (XBOX 360 version)

by Pixel1243
https://github.com/woerldonz-pixel/UMVC3_NX

A static recompilation of Ultimate Marvel vs Capcom 3

Although a lot of work has been done on my part to get the game up to my standard performance wise

This has used reNut-NX Ultimate Switch 360 Port Base as template/base

https://github.com/ChanseyIsTheBest/renut_nx_ultimate_base/tree/main
https://gbatemp.net/threads/renut-nx-ultimate-switch-360-port-base.686515/

So credit also to contributors of that template

You will need your own disk of Ultimate Marvel vs Capcom 3 (XBOX 360 version) to play this game

Your UMVC3 folder should be put in the switch directory with the following umvc3.nro, the renderer's shaders (deko3d_shaders.bin, deko3d_glsl.bin) and the game files in game_root/. Start umvc3.nro with a title takeover (hold R while launching an installed game) or a forwarder with full memory (i used the forwarder); the album applet does not give the game enough memory. The game writes katamari.toml (your settings) at its first start.

Recommended settings for performance
1785 MHz, GPU at 768 MHz and ram at 1600 MHZ which can be set with sys-clk

I tested on my nintendo switch and it appears to run at 60fps most of the time

Known issues:
Game might sometimes show corrupt/missing graphics while playing though, if this happens i recommend resetting the console the clear the GPU or/and re-copying the game disc files to the SD card again. Personally im not sure what causes that however you may have a better experience, since i couldnt find any actual bugs reported on my logs about the issue
